  "task": {
    "objective": "Install one block at each side station and two at the middle station. Cargo cannot be carried upward on ladders; raise it on shared lifts. Build a bridge to support the middle station. A station's corresponding role earns the larger installation bonus even when another worker carries the material.",
    "natural_termination": "All station_count entries equal station_required [1,1,2]. Otherwise truncate after 160 nonterminal steps. Natural completion takes precedence at the horizon. Impact immobilization is bounded at two future calls unless another impact occurs. Terminal raw state is absorbing.",
    "interaction": "Opposite-pad resting blocks and bracing workers support a loaded lift. Another worker removing ballast or stopping a brace can make the platform drop and stun its riders. A crank operator raises or safely lowers platforms; the shared brake also stops useful motion. Physical material can be installed privately, left as ballast, or bolted into traversable support at three bridge cells. Reclaiming bridge material removes that support and can drop another worker.",
    "observation_access": "The side-view map, ladder and solid-cell legend, all workers, blocks, platforms, ballast pads, stations, crane state and events are public. All entity visibility masks are true. Every displayed changing attribute is returned in the flat observation. Downward screen y is gravity. Loose waist-high cargo permits worker co-location; bolted blocks and lift platforms are solid cells."
  },
